<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

	<PropertyGroup Label="NugetProperties">
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
		<PackageId>Kebechet.Blazor.EventHandlers.ShortClick</PackageId>
		<Description>Contains @onshortclick blazor event handler, and an opt-in click mode that gives @onclick the same short-click semantics</Description>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Kebechet/Blazor.EventHandlers.ShortClick</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Kebechet/Blazor.EventHandlers.ShortClick</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<Version>3.1.0</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>Added an opt-in click mode: with data-shortclick-mode="click" on &lt;html&gt;, &lt;body&gt; or any element, a click that a pointer made reaches the page only when its press was a short click, so a plain @onclick behaves like @onshortclick. A press held for 400ms or longer, or moved past the threshold, loses its click and the click's default action. Keyboard and programmatic clicks always pass, and text-entry controls are exempt. Off by default; @onshortclick is unchanged. Also added data-shortclick-long-press-ms: how long a press may be held and still be a short click (default 400ms), for @onshortclick and click mode alike, from the nearest element carrying it; a value that is not a positive number falls back to 400. Fixed: a press is timed by its events' own timestamps, so a quick tap released while the main thread is busy (a WebAssembly render) is no longer taken for a long press; every pointer is tracked on its own, one gesture raises at most one shortclick, touch, mouse and pen presses are tracked apart, and a cancelled press is forgotten.</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\..\LICENSE">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Include="..\..\README.md">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="8.0.6" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
